infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When RSC pays — and when SPA + REST still wins
  desc The architecture-review tradeoff: RSC charges a real complexity tax that only some product shapes repay
  compares
    - label Reach for RSC
      children
        - label Content- & data-heavy pages
          desc Structure matches the product, so the model earns its cost
        - label Bundle-sensitive audiences
          desc Zero-bundle server components cut the JS shipped to clients
        - label Large teams
          desc The enforced data/UI split pays off across many developers
        - label Already paying for SSR
          desc The server tier RSC needs is already in production
        - label Tax: two execution environments
          desc Leak-prone serialization boundary, framework coupling, harder debug
    - label Keep SPA + REST
      children
        - label Login-gated dashboard
          desc Bundle is cached after first visit, so RSC buys little
        - label SEO is irrelevant
          desc No crawlability gain to justify the migration
        - label Small team shipping
          desc One mental model keeps velocity high
        - label No SSR tier yet
          desc Avoid standing up server infrastructure just for RSC
        - label Win: one mental model
          desc No two-environment boundary that can leak or throw
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
